   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-03-06">March 6, 1942.</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs>,<lb/>
               Union Theological Seminary,<lb/> Broadway at 120th Street,<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York, N.Y., U.S.A.</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I am enclosing a copy of a review of your pamphlet <q>War Aims</q>, which appeared
            in our college Daily, this week. I thought you may be interested in seeing what the students
            wrote, concerning you.</p>
            <p>I have shown the pamphlet to a number of students, and it has created a great deal of
               interest – so much so that one group has ordered 25 copies.</p>
            <p>With best wishes to you personally, I am,</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Yours very sincerely,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1226" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Edward Lute</hi></rs></signed><lb/>
               ETL: EW<lb/>
               Encl.
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
